issue.body:
This is a stylistic question as much as a bug. We have a lot of code that looks like the following and since upgrading to the latest eslint are experiencing indentation errors that are unexpected. Is the formatting that eslint expects in this scenario the desired result. It seems strange to me. 

I've provided a simple reproducible example below using eslint 1.3.1.

``` js
var Q = require('q');

function test() {
    return Q.fcall(function () {
        return true;
    }).then(function (result) {
        return result;
    }, function (err) {
        if (err) {
            throw new Error(err);
        }
    });
}

test();
```

``` json
{
  "rules": {
    "indent": [2, 4]
  }
}
```

``` sh
$ eslint --version
v1.3.1
$ eslint .

index.js
   9:9  error  Expected indentation of 12 space characters but found 8  indent
  12:5  error  Expected indentation of 8 space characters but found 4   indent

✖ 2 problems (2 errors, 0 warnings)

```

